			<div class="content" id="post-content-2486606">
									

<p>Overall, I enjoyed this one. I like the idea of prosthetic limbs that were rushed out the door and didn't do what they were supposed to do. The background in the addenda demonstrates that admirably without being boring to read. I enjoyed that there was a character that said no to a secretive organisation messing with the anomalous that wasn't murdered or otherwise killed by his erstwhile comrades.</p>
<p>I did find the overt Star Wars references a bit jarring though. I could see there being someone with a sense of humour making a SKYWALKER protocol, but then to have the Anderson robotics guy make a direct reference to Vader as well kind of feels a little far. On top of that, there's two robot themed MTFs noted in the article too, so it lends the whole thing a strangely wacky tone for a piece about malfunctioning robotic limbs and a pending biotech arms race based on mechanical enhancement.</p>

